{title: Lord While For All Mankind We Pray}
{artist: John Reynell Wreford}
{key: G}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: 100}

Verse 1
Lord, while for all mankind we pray, Of every clime and coast,
Oh, hear us for our native land, The land we love the most.

Verse 2
Oh, guard our shores from every foe, With peace our borders bless,
With prosp'rous times our cities crown, Our fields with plenteousness.

Verse 3
Unite us in the sacred love Of knowledge, truth and Thee;
And let our hills and valleys shout The songs of liberty.

Verse 4
Here may religion, pure and mild, Smile on our Sabbath hours;
And piety and virtue bless The home of us and ours.

Verse 5
Lord of the nations, Thus to Thee Our country we commend;
Be Thou her Refuge and her Trust, Her everlasting Friend.
